==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|ātorcoppe||spider}}, corresponding to {{compound|atter|gloss1=poison, venom|cop|gloss2=head|lang=en}}. The latter is still to be found in the English word {{m|en|cobweb}}. Cognate to Dutch {{m|nl|etterkop||peevish or ill-natured person}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈætəkɒp/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# ''(obsolete except in dialects)'' A [[spider]].
# ''(obsolete except in dialects)'' A [[peevish]] or [[ill-natured]] person.

